WEBVTT

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:14.889
<i>Bamboo</i>

00:00:14.973 --> 00:00:18.685
<i>Laundry-hanging rods</i>

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:24.315
<i>Bamboo, laundry-hanging rods</i>

00:00:27.026 --> 00:00:28.361
I'm home.

00:00:40.749 --> 00:00:45.962
<i>Bamboo, laundry-hanging rods</i>

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:30.256
UNCLE:
YOU'RE FINE THE WAY YOU ARE

00:02:01.496 --> 00:02:03.164
GET HOME

00:02:08.378 --> 00:02:09.420
SOLD CHEAPER THAN A SCOURING PAD

00:02:16.511 --> 00:02:17.720
75 MINUTES AGO

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:19.764
Fujimiya said she's coming later.

00:02:20.515 --> 00:02:21.891
Got it.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:26.521
What?

00:02:26.604 --> 00:02:29.482
Well, she is a nice girl.

00:02:29.566 --> 00:02:31.901
Guess so.

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:35.530
<i>She tried to cut you out of my life.</i>

00:02:35.613 --> 00:02:37.490
TO THE UNCLE FROM ANOTHER WORLD

00:02:38.116 --> 00:02:39.200
You've got mail.

00:02:39.284 --> 00:02:41.995
I know, but it's in English,
so I ignored it.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:47.750
Let's see.
"Changes to the YouTube Partner Program."

00:02:48.793 --> 00:02:50.628
Didn't know you read English fluently.

00:02:50.712 --> 00:02:52.630
No, I pasted it into a translation app.

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:55.717
How convenient.

00:02:56.801 --> 00:02:58.219
And? What does it say?

00:03:00.138 --> 00:03:02.932
Uncle, you're about to lose your job.

00:03:04.976 --> 00:03:05.977
What?

00:03:07.729 --> 00:03:10.106
<i>Early 2018.</i>

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:14.068
<i>Many small YouTubers lost ad revenue.</i>

00:03:14.152 --> 00:03:15.570
1,000 SUBSCRIBERS OR 4,000 HOURS

00:03:15.653 --> 00:03:18.448
<i>My uncle's channel wasn't no exception.</i>

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:20.909
STARTING BY FEBRUARY 20, 2018

00:03:20.992 --> 00:03:23.369
FEBRUARY 19TH, MONDAY

00:03:25.496 --> 00:03:28.583
By the end of today,
I need to reach 4,000 hours of watch time

00:03:28.666 --> 00:03:31.377
and 1,000 subscribers.

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:33.796
UNCLE FROM ANOTHER WORLD
CHANNEL SUBSCRIBERS

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.506
812 PEOPLE

00:03:36.299 --> 00:03:38.843
<i>The watch time greatly exceeds</i>
<i>the threshold.</i>

00:03:38.927 --> 00:03:41.471
<i>Why so few subscribers?</i>

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:46.809
MIKECHAN: I JUST FOUND
YOUR CHANNEL! AMAZING CGI!

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:49.270
UNCLE FROM ANOTHER WORLD
IT'S NOT CGI. IT'S REAL MAGIC.

00:03:49.354 --> 00:03:52.232
PLEASE READ THE DESCRIPTION
BEFORE YOU WATCH THE VIDEOS.

00:03:52.315 --> 00:03:54.943
RECENTLY, I'M IRKED
BECAUSE MANY PEOPLE COMMENT

00:03:55.026 --> 00:03:56.110
WITHOUT READING IT.

00:03:56.194 --> 00:03:57.820
PLEASE MAKE THE INTERNET
AN ENJOYABLE PLACE

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:59.155
BY COMPLYING WITH THE RULES.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:01.491
@UNCLEFROMANOTHERWORLD
UM, SURE

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:02.825
THERE HE GOES AGAIN

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:05.495
I'M DONE BEING YOUR FAN
ARE YOU TODAY YEARS OLD?

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:08.414
AGAIN POPS IS RED IN THE FACE
HE MAKES UP HIS OWN RULES

00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:15.588
-This is why!
-What?

00:04:15.672 --> 00:04:19.717
Your fans are unsubscribing
because of your shitty replies!

00:04:19.801 --> 00:04:22.512
But, Takafumi…

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:24.097
No buts!

00:04:25.181 --> 00:04:29.560
-Anyway, we are in a tight spot.
-Yes, we've got to figure something out.

00:04:29.644 --> 00:04:35.024
I haven't been like this
since the Sealed City, Luvaldram.

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:39.028
Their defense magic was broken,
and 1,000 legendary beasts were released.

00:04:44.867 --> 00:04:46.202
Uncle,

00:04:47.328 --> 00:04:50.999
why do you mention such a fascinating tale
in a moment of crisis?

00:04:51.082 --> 00:04:52.667
Do you want me to tell you?

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:54.711
Of course I do.

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:56.087
In a moment of crisis?

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:58.006
It's your fault!

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:00.341
<i>Icuras elran</i>.

00:05:02.051 --> 00:05:04.679
Is this the Sealed City?

00:05:10.351 --> 00:05:12.353
What an enormous barrier.

00:05:13.438 --> 00:05:15.481
What is it blocking?

00:05:16.065 --> 00:05:17.984
You don't know anything, do you?

00:05:19.277 --> 00:05:21.654
Do you have the brains of an orc?

00:05:22.572 --> 00:05:24.324
An orc?

00:05:24.407 --> 00:05:25.867
-Orc.
-It's an orc!

00:05:28.202 --> 00:05:29.787
Do not panic.

00:05:29.871 --> 00:05:31.664
Yes, he looks exactly like an orc.

00:05:32.248 --> 00:05:33.916
But if he were a real orc,

00:05:34.625 --> 00:05:37.378
he would have perished
the moment he stepped within the barrier.

00:05:37.462 --> 00:05:40.131
-That's true.
-Is he still a human?

00:05:40.214 --> 00:05:41.632
This world is ending.

00:05:41.716 --> 00:05:43.009
I agree.

00:05:46.888 --> 00:05:49.682
Orc face, you're often in a spot
as if hemmed in by Chu's army.

00:05:49.766 --> 00:05:50.767
Wait.

00:05:52.685 --> 00:05:54.020
Hemmed in by Chu's army?

00:05:54.103 --> 00:05:56.230
<i>The Elf girl used an idiom</i>
<i>referencing Chu.</i>

00:05:56.314 --> 00:05:58.316
<i>Wasn't Chu an ancient state in China?</i>

00:05:58.399 --> 00:05:59.984
<i>It must be the translation.</i>

00:06:01.069 --> 00:06:02.945
LANGUAGE MENU
1 JAPANESE - 2 GRANBAHAMAL

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:04.238
<i>Irg zag lar rarla…</i>

00:06:04.322 --> 00:06:08.493
The verbatim translation is
"Wail of Guben's army on the 10th day."

00:06:08.576 --> 00:06:11.412
It doesn't make sense as is,
so the magic adapted Japanese nicely.

00:06:11.496 --> 00:06:12.705
What is this interface?

00:06:13.414 --> 00:06:15.666
I copied this feature
from your video player.

00:06:16.751 --> 00:06:18.544
Don't you want to hide your face?

00:06:19.587 --> 00:06:20.630
No.

00:06:22.965 --> 00:06:27.637
It doesn't make me want to retch anymore
now that I'm used to it.

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:30.932
-I can tolerate…
-Wow, a giant fruit.

00:06:32.767 --> 00:06:35.019
It's an <i>equa</i>, a produce of the South.

00:06:35.103 --> 00:06:36.687
SEALED CITY LUVALDRAM
THE LAND WHERE BEASTS RISE

00:06:36.771 --> 00:06:39.273
<i>This barrier protecting the city</i>
<i>wards off mythical beasts</i>

00:06:39.357 --> 00:06:43.152
that dwell in the west
of the Land Where Beasts Rise.

00:06:43.986 --> 00:06:47.240
A barrier of this scale
isn't built in one night.

00:06:47.323 --> 00:06:49.534
-<i>Kilighd l'gid riolran…</i>
-The city's been a trading hub…

00:06:49.617 --> 00:06:52.245
-<i>…Kulosha l'gid riolran.</i>
-…for local goods,

00:06:52.328 --> 00:06:54.080
all thanks to this barrier!

00:07:01.003 --> 00:07:02.171
Look at the barrier!

00:07:05.842 --> 00:07:07.969
What did you do, Uncle?

00:07:08.553 --> 00:07:11.222
I wanted to see if it would work.

00:07:23.234 --> 00:07:25.361
-Look!
-Beasts are coming!

00:07:25.445 --> 00:07:26.904
The cyclops!

00:07:26.988 --> 00:07:29.115
That's a Titan!

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:41.335
Can that be a cloud dragon?

00:07:41.419 --> 00:07:42.712
Bring the spell cards!

00:07:42.795 --> 00:07:43.963
Which ones?

00:07:44.046 --> 00:07:45.339
All of them!

00:07:49.218 --> 00:07:51.888
I've only seen such terrifying monsters
in the picture books

00:07:52.638 --> 00:07:53.931
from my hometown.

00:08:01.397 --> 00:08:04.066
Approximately 1,000 monsters.

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:06.277
What do you think, orc face?

00:08:06.777 --> 00:08:09.113
There are too many for us to handle.

00:08:10.114 --> 00:08:12.033
We cannot prevent mass casualty.

00:08:12.533 --> 00:08:13.618
That's correct.

00:08:35.765 --> 00:08:36.974
What an ugly face.

00:08:39.227 --> 00:08:40.853
But you don't hide it.

00:08:45.858 --> 00:08:47.068
You are so awkward.

00:08:50.154 --> 00:08:51.197
Such a fool.

00:08:52.406 --> 00:08:53.449
Run.

00:09:15.096 --> 00:09:16.222
<i>I put it up again.</i>

00:09:16.305 --> 00:09:17.515
What?

00:09:17.598 --> 00:09:22.186
I asked the barrier-forming spirits
to repair it and they did.

00:09:22.937 --> 00:09:25.648
The spirits gave me
a hell of a time for it.

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:27.525
<i>A hell of a time?</i>

00:09:30.403 --> 00:09:32.780
We lived!

00:09:32.863 --> 00:09:34.865
But what was that?

00:09:34.949 --> 00:09:37.243
I thought I saw something flashing.

00:09:37.827 --> 00:09:40.288
Does it mean someone broke the seal?

00:09:40.371 --> 00:09:41.956
Was it a beast?

00:09:42.039 --> 00:09:43.416
A beast?

00:09:57.513 --> 00:09:59.265
You dropped this, Elf girl.

00:09:59.348 --> 00:10:02.143
Thank you. It's ancient.

00:10:02.226 --> 00:10:05.688
It's a legendary weapon, right?
You've got to handle it carefully.

00:10:05.771 --> 00:10:08.232
"Legendary sword" sounds cool,

00:10:08.941 --> 00:10:11.152
but, at the end of the day,
it's an antique.

00:10:12.737 --> 00:10:14.697
An antique.

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:17.116
The barrier's not so different.

00:10:17.199 --> 00:10:19.619
No maintenance was performed
for several centuries.

00:10:19.702 --> 00:10:21.829
Some failure is inevitable.

00:10:21.912 --> 00:10:24.832
I heard that barrier magic books
are in the king's capital.

00:10:28.836 --> 00:10:31.464
What a close call, orc face.

00:10:33.132 --> 00:10:36.260
Why don't you tell them
that I broke the barrier?

00:10:41.182 --> 00:10:43.392
You owe me dinner.

00:10:44.852 --> 00:10:46.395
We'll call it even then.

00:10:57.031 --> 00:10:58.240
<i>I took off.</i>

00:10:58.324 --> 00:10:59.950
Why the hell you did run?

00:11:00.701 --> 00:11:02.828
It's critical to deter
these types of jerks

00:11:02.912 --> 00:11:05.665
from extorting on the very first attempt.

00:11:06.248 --> 00:11:08.584
<i>Otherwise, you'll be a sucker forever.</i>

00:11:08.668 --> 00:11:12.713
All right, orc face.
Next, fetch me some pastries.

00:11:13.297 --> 00:11:16.300
<i>His skepticism runs deep.</i>

00:11:18.302 --> 00:11:22.556
Ask the spirits.

00:11:25.726 --> 00:11:26.936
What are you doing?

00:11:27.019 --> 00:11:31.107
I thought I'd ask my viewers to subscribe.

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:32.691
What?

00:11:32.775 --> 00:11:37.488
I explained I need them to help
by subscribing to my channel.

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:40.825
What a stupid thing you've done!

00:11:40.908 --> 00:11:42.576
You're done if you show your weakness.

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:45.413
Those trolls will start a flame war
and grill you to the bone.

00:11:45.496 --> 00:11:48.499
Internet trolls who make money from hating
will come after you.

00:11:48.582 --> 00:11:50.418
You are finished!

00:11:50.501 --> 00:11:52.628
Uncle, you are so done!

00:12:00.636 --> 00:12:02.138
I SUBSCRIBED. KEEP GOING!

00:12:02.221 --> 00:12:03.222
SINCE YOU ASKED…

00:12:04.432 --> 00:12:05.433
You guys…

00:12:05.516 --> 00:12:07.518
AWAITING UPDATES
I'M ROOTING FOR YOU

00:12:09.562 --> 00:12:10.688
Unbelievable.

00:12:10.771 --> 00:12:15.401
<i>I had only seen the worst</i>
<i>of the social media community.</i>

00:12:16.068 --> 00:12:21.031
<i>The Internet had a kind</i>
<i>and supportive side I hadn't seen before.</i>

00:12:22.408 --> 00:12:23.742
Hello!

00:12:26.537 --> 00:12:29.665
<i>Who's the skeptic here?</i>

00:12:30.499 --> 00:12:33.794
Wow, we reached 1,000 subscribers! Yes!

00:12:35.212 --> 00:12:38.048
"Thank you, everyone."

00:12:38.632 --> 00:12:40.551
Should I use a smiley emoji?

00:12:41.594 --> 00:12:42.595
Sure.

00:12:44.513 --> 00:12:45.514
What's going on?

00:12:46.348 --> 00:12:47.933
ORC FACE QUICKLY TRANSFORM

00:12:49.727 --> 00:12:53.397
<i>The aging, unemployed singles</i>
<i>are becoming a serious social problem.</i>

00:12:53.981 --> 00:12:56.984
For example, an unemployed uncle
crashing at his nephew's place,

00:12:57.067 --> 00:12:59.069
wrecking the young man's life.

00:12:59.862 --> 00:13:01.113
Unthinkable, right?

00:13:01.197 --> 00:13:02.698
I totally agree.

00:13:03.365 --> 00:13:07.411
Wow, the new video
already reached 10,000 views.

00:13:09.246 --> 00:13:12.541
Is being a YouTuber considered a career?

00:13:12.625 --> 00:13:14.877
The revenue comes only from ads, right?

00:13:15.377 --> 00:13:17.004
Yeah.

00:13:17.588 --> 00:13:19.798
That's a commonly asked question.

00:13:20.382 --> 00:13:23.385
I'm a pro
collaborating with a corporation,

00:13:23.469 --> 00:13:25.471
so I can't disclose the details.

00:13:26.096 --> 00:13:27.306
Sorry.

00:13:29.016 --> 00:13:30.684
With a roommate…

00:13:32.895 --> 00:13:37.107
Takafumi can't even consider
living with a girlfriend.

00:13:39.401 --> 00:13:43.364
Oh, yeah, Fujimiya. You should live here.

00:13:45.115 --> 00:13:47.076
Takafumi's room sleeps two.

00:13:47.159 --> 00:13:48.536
Wait!

00:13:48.619 --> 00:13:50.496
-I don't mind sleeping on the floor.
-Wait!

00:13:50.579 --> 00:13:52.998
Having two men in my room is a bit tight.

00:13:53.832 --> 00:13:55.543
It's not that spacious.

00:13:55.626 --> 00:13:56.627
Really?

00:14:01.298 --> 00:14:03.133
Sorry, I need to go out for a bit.

00:14:03.217 --> 00:14:05.302
What? Wait!

00:14:05.386 --> 00:14:08.097
Sugarless jam, 198 yen.

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:13.060
That Takafumi.

00:14:14.186 --> 00:14:18.691
Despite a wonderful girl such as you
showing interest in him,

00:14:18.774 --> 00:14:21.068
he only sees you as a friend.

00:14:23.153 --> 00:14:25.531
Did something happen in the past?

00:14:26.991 --> 00:14:27.992
Huh?

00:14:28.576 --> 00:14:30.578
-You can talk to me.
-No, thank you.

00:14:32.413 --> 00:14:35.499
Surely my experience of sacrificing
my love countless times means something.

00:14:35.583 --> 00:14:37.251
Kaede, at least go with my hands.

00:14:37.334 --> 00:14:39.211
<i>Surely there are things</i>
<i>only I can tell you.</i>

00:14:39.295 --> 00:14:40.671
No way!

00:14:40.754 --> 00:14:44.133
I have nothing to confide to someone whose
experience only comes from video games.

00:14:53.893 --> 00:14:56.896
I'm not good enough for you.

00:15:00.608 --> 00:15:02.735
<i>He is a weirdo.</i>

00:15:03.235 --> 00:15:07.990
<i>But he has good intentions</i>
<i>to try to bring us together.</i>

00:15:09.950 --> 00:15:13.329
I was too harsh earlier.

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:17.791
What?

00:15:17.875 --> 00:15:20.252
Who… are you?

00:15:20.336 --> 00:15:23.255
I am Takafumi's aunt.

00:15:23.339 --> 00:15:24.548
His aunt?

00:15:24.632 --> 00:15:27.217
Why is his aunt here?

00:15:27.301 --> 00:15:31.680
His uncle is here. Why not his aunt?

00:15:33.557 --> 00:15:35.267
Where is Uncle?

00:15:35.351 --> 00:15:36.435
He's in the bathroom.

00:15:37.728 --> 00:15:39.480
Help me, Spirit of Sound.

00:15:41.732 --> 00:15:42.858
I'm here.

00:15:43.442 --> 00:15:45.361
Okay, let's talk.

00:15:45.444 --> 00:15:47.571
-I mean, let's have a chat.
-What?

00:15:47.655 --> 00:15:51.492
It's time for girl talk.
No need to hold back.

00:15:51.575 --> 00:15:53.577
So, tell me, what happened in the past?

00:15:53.661 --> 00:15:57.039
Nothing. Seriously, nothing happened.

00:15:59.291 --> 00:16:00.668
I'm back.

00:16:08.133 --> 00:16:10.594
AND HERE WE ARE NOW

00:16:12.721 --> 00:16:14.348
It's Takafumi.

00:16:14.431 --> 00:16:16.809
Your aunt wants to give me
relationship advice.

00:16:16.892 --> 00:16:18.727
What? My aunt?

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:20.771
<i>Relationship advice?</i>

00:16:26.151 --> 00:16:27.361
Uncle?

00:16:27.444 --> 00:16:28.946
No, I'm your aunt.

00:16:29.905 --> 00:16:31.240
Sonic and Tailz are--

00:16:31.323 --> 00:16:34.076
No, it's Tails with an S.

00:16:34.159 --> 00:16:37.413
His real name is Miles Prower, but
he goes by "Tails," as he has two tails.

00:16:37.496 --> 00:16:38.956
-Uncle.
-I'm your aunt.

00:16:40.958 --> 00:16:44.712
You could have used this magic to change
your appearance in the other world.

00:16:44.795 --> 00:16:46.338
Don't make it sound easy.

00:16:46.964 --> 00:16:50.175
The mind gradually changes
to conform to the body.

00:16:51.260 --> 00:16:54.722
There is a risk
that I can lose my identity.

00:16:57.224 --> 00:16:59.268
Unless absolutely necessary,

00:16:59.351 --> 00:17:01.729
this magic is forbidden!

00:17:02.354 --> 00:17:04.314
<i>And you are using it for a girl talk.</i>

00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:05.941
Well…

00:17:06.692 --> 00:17:09.153
Whatever. Let's shoot a YouTube video.

00:17:11.447 --> 00:17:13.824
No, now's not the time.

00:17:13.907 --> 00:17:16.618
Fujimiya is here,
so we should entertain her.

00:17:16.702 --> 00:17:18.954
Let's shoot a gaming video
with Guardian Heroes.

00:17:19.038 --> 00:17:20.456
I'll do it!

00:17:20.539 --> 00:17:23.959
I've been wanting to shoot a gaming video.

00:17:24.043 --> 00:17:26.420
Yay!

00:17:26.503 --> 00:17:29.506
We don't have time,
so keep your face like that.

00:17:29.590 --> 00:17:31.967
All right, let's get started.

00:17:33.635 --> 00:17:34.678
What is going on?

00:17:37.431 --> 00:17:40.017
All right.
The video is successfully uploaded.

00:17:40.100 --> 00:17:43.979
I'm not as good as I once was
but kept an entertaining play style.

00:17:44.063 --> 00:17:46.273
I think we'll get tons of likes.

00:17:46.356 --> 00:17:47.983
Can I see the video?

00:17:48.067 --> 00:17:51.361
Uncle, before we get to that,
we need to entertain Fujimiya.

00:17:51.445 --> 00:17:53.280
Right, I forgot.

00:17:53.363 --> 00:17:55.449
Uncle? Not aunt?

00:17:56.742 --> 00:17:57.743
All right.

00:17:57.826 --> 00:18:01.789
Let's review Takafumi and Fujimiya's
earliest encounters.

00:18:01.872 --> 00:18:03.916
You cut right to the chase, Uncle.

00:18:03.999 --> 00:18:05.793
Let's start, Takafumi.

00:18:05.876 --> 00:18:09.171
Spirit of Memory,
show me a fragment of the recollections.

00:18:13.175 --> 00:18:15.511
-What the heck is this?
-It's magic.

00:18:15.594 --> 00:18:17.888
Stop kidding me.

00:18:17.971 --> 00:18:20.349
Oh, this must be a hologram! Right?

00:18:20.849 --> 00:18:22.851
I've seen this in movies.

00:18:25.646 --> 00:18:27.106
Yeah.

00:18:27.189 --> 00:18:29.691
This Sony machine projects the image here.

00:18:30.275 --> 00:18:32.861
So it's by Sony.

00:18:34.196 --> 00:18:37.282
That's our elementary school
before it was renovated.

00:18:39.368 --> 00:18:42.496
<i>I bet you have erotic magazines</i>
<i>stashed at home!</i>

00:18:42.579 --> 00:18:44.498
<i>I don't have them.</i>

00:18:45.541 --> 00:18:49.002
Wow, I want one of these devices.

00:18:49.086 --> 00:18:51.672
<i>Don't talk back to me!</i>

00:18:51.755 --> 00:18:54.883
<i>-Crap bomb punches!</i>
<i>-Ouch, ouch!</i>

00:18:55.467 --> 00:18:58.428
Strange. Where is Fujimiya?

00:18:58.512 --> 00:19:00.514
There's only a filthy brat.

00:19:01.014 --> 00:19:02.349
That's you, Fujimiya.

00:19:03.851 --> 00:19:04.852
What?

00:19:11.859 --> 00:19:14.319
Oh, I see. Yeah, that makes sense.

00:19:14.403 --> 00:19:17.614
<i>What? Was I really like this?</i>

00:19:18.615 --> 00:19:21.326
<i>I thought we had</i>
<i>a more bittersweet childhood together.</i>

00:19:25.998 --> 00:19:27.416
<i>Here's poop.</i>

00:19:27.499 --> 00:19:28.834
Wait, what?

00:19:30.127 --> 00:19:31.628
Fujimiya, I'm so sorry.

00:19:32.337 --> 00:19:33.630
This is hopeless.

00:19:33.714 --> 00:19:35.632
Don't watch it!

00:19:35.716 --> 00:19:39.595
Incredible of Takafumi to notice you
when he saw you on the street.

00:19:39.678 --> 00:19:42.764
Of course I would.

00:19:47.060 --> 00:19:48.729
I wouldn't forget Fujimiya.

00:19:54.776 --> 00:19:56.486
Yeah, right.

00:19:56.570 --> 00:19:58.155
Ouch. What's this for?

00:19:59.072 --> 00:20:00.115
I see.

00:20:07.831 --> 00:20:10.709
It's not about the appearance.

00:20:12.502 --> 00:20:15.714
Had I been able to see that, maybe…

00:20:16.340 --> 00:20:17.382
Oh, no.

00:20:18.217 --> 00:20:20.302
Is this body affecting my mind?

00:20:21.428 --> 00:20:23.055
<i>Please stop, Mr. Fujimiya.</i>

00:20:23.138 --> 00:20:25.390
-You called me Mr. Fujimiya.
-<i>Poop, poop!</i>

00:20:25.474 --> 00:20:28.435
I seriously thought you were a boy
for a while after we met.

00:20:28.518 --> 00:20:29.937
That's horrible!

00:20:34.066 --> 00:20:35.734
That's the video we uploaded just now.

00:20:35.817 --> 00:20:37.778
VIRTUAL ELF YOUTUBER UNCLE

00:20:37.861 --> 00:20:39.154
Virtual what?

00:20:39.780 --> 00:20:43.158
<i>Hi, guys! It's Uncle here.</i>

00:20:43.242 --> 00:20:46.411
<i>Today, I want to do something</i>
<i>a little different.</i>

00:20:46.495 --> 00:20:48.914
<i>Ta-da! I want to play a SEGA SATURN game,</i>

00:20:48.997 --> 00:20:52.417
<i>Guardian Heroes!</i>

00:20:52.501 --> 00:20:54.253
<i>Clap, clap, clap.</i>

00:20:55.212 --> 00:20:57.214
<i>All right, for this video,</i>

00:20:57.297 --> 00:21:00.842
<i>I'll play up to obtaining</i>
<i>the hero's sword.</i>

00:21:00.926 --> 00:21:05.806
<i>To obtain the sword of Han's hero,</i>
<i>select the bottom answer twice.</i>

00:21:05.889 --> 00:21:07.432
<i>Yep, it's that simple.</i>

00:21:07.516 --> 00:21:08.892
<i>All right, now…</i>

00:21:08.976 --> 00:21:10.686
Wait a minute, Takafumi.

00:21:11.812 --> 00:21:15.107
My game's screen isn't shown at all
in the video we just shot.

00:21:15.190 --> 00:21:16.650
Why would anyone watch this?

00:21:16.733 --> 00:21:18.360
Look at the view count. There's only…

00:21:18.443 --> 00:21:19.861
NEW: VIRTUAL ELF YOUTUBER UNCLE

00:21:20.946 --> 00:21:22.072
…200,000 views?

00:21:23.865 --> 00:21:25.575
We're going viral!

00:21:25.659 --> 00:21:28.245
This will be record-breaking!
We'll hit three million views!

00:21:28.328 --> 00:21:30.372
People don't want to watch
a frowsy, old geezer!

00:21:30.455 --> 00:21:34.001
It's the age of virtual YouTubers!
Hot girl avatars!

00:21:36.295 --> 00:21:37.671
SHIMA ARASHI: CUTE!

00:21:37.754 --> 00:21:40.132
I'M A FAN - TOO CUTE

00:21:40.215 --> 00:21:43.093
NO NEED FOR A GAME CONSOLE

00:21:48.682 --> 00:21:50.309
You are all the same.

00:21:57.149 --> 00:22:00.027
-Yes! I was spot-on!
-His nasty face appeared!

00:22:00.110 --> 00:22:01.737
No!

00:22:01.820 --> 00:22:03.572
-We did it!
-Gross!

00:22:03.655 --> 00:22:06.825
No!

00:22:06.908 --> 00:22:10.954
<i>Uncle's pride as a YouTuber</i>
<i>was torn to pieces.</i>

00:22:13.123 --> 00:22:16.501
<i>But on the payout date,</i>

00:22:16.585 --> 00:22:19.713
<i>a deluxe sashimi plate was served</i>
<i>on our dinner table.</i>

00:23:46.716 --> 00:23:50.929
